  "notes": "MoE backend P3b (tasks/m23-spec.md M23-D7, shipped default): the CERE_MOE_BACKEND=p3b library, routed experts on the vendored FlashInfer 0.6.17 SM120 CUTLASS fused MoE with per-m-bucket pinned deterministic GEMM1/GEMM2 tactic pairs (M23-D6), each bit-equal to the K7 reference at block level; promoted by the identity gate (native_hashes identical to K7's on the D9 parity set). Deterministic at rows = 1 without cache (K8/X11 repeat evidence); NVFP4 W4A4 and fp8_e4m3 KV; MoE scales as flashinfer_cutlass (Q14), N experts with up != gate scale. The in-process CERE executor (libcere_executor.so, ABI v4) on GPU0: up to 16 rows (tasks/m23-spec.md P8; 4 before), text in and out (tool calls parsed by CERE as SGLang's qwen3_coder detector; stop strings matched by CERE), no prefix cache. Rows are concurrently decoded sessions in one batched decode step, bit-identical to each session decoded as one row (M2.6 C/K evidence); prefill is serialized, one 4,096-token chunk of one session per round, alternating with decode rounds (prefill row_counts [1]). Greedy decoding (temperature < 1e-6 or top_k 1 with neutral processors) runs the unchanged greedy path; sampled decoding (temperature, top_p, top_k, min_p, seed, frequency/presence/repetition penalties, logit_bias) and logprobs with top_logprobs up to 20 run the M2.7 device sampler, which the library must report (native_sampler 1, checked at start). Each row of a batched decode step samples with its own sampling, output counts and counter key (its session position; ledger CR4), so a sampled session commits the same tokens at rows 1-4 whatever else shares the round. The sampler is checked against its own logits and its CPU reference only: it is not an SGLang parity claim (G1 has not passed), and seeded outputs are reproducible on this artifact and library, not SGLang's sequence. n > 1 runs n sessions as rows (n <= 4, no session turn or continue mode); sampled choice i >= 1 draws with a distinct per-choice seed (ledger M8 channels (2, 3)). Grammar (M2.8): response_format json_object/json_schema (dialect json-schema-2020-12/xgrammar-0.2.1, the listed keywords only; numeric bounds only on integer schemas in enforced forms), top-level regex and ebnf, and tool_choice required/named or a strict tool (tool_calls_constrained) are enforced in the executor: the grammar process (xgrammar 0.2.1, sidecar --role grammar) supplies per-position vocab masks, which the library must accept (native_token_mask 1, checked at start), and the executor masks the scored row after penalties and before logit_bias (K12, SGLang order); a constrained row waits for its mask each decode round (ledger CR5) and constrained tickets never speculate (I3); one constraint per request, greedy or sampled, rows as text decoding; outputs are not post-validated, and this is not a throughput claim. verify, snapshot/restore, images and prompts over the context limit are absent and therefore refused. Not a throughput or capacity claim.",
